<h1>List &amp; Label Cross Platform – Blazor WASM Sample</h1>

<p>
    This sample demonstrates how to use
    <strong>List &amp; Label Cross Platform (LLCP)</strong> inside a
    <strong>standalone Blazor WebAssembly</strong> application.
</p>

<h2>Architecture</h2>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Pure client-side</strong> — no ASP.NET Core backend is required.
        LLCP runs entirely inside the browser via WebAssembly.
    </li>
    <li>
        The <strong>SkiaSharp</strong> rendering engine is loaded as a
        <code>SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.WebAssembly</code> package, which provides
        a native WASM binary that LLCP uses to render PDF pages.
    </li>
    <li>
        The report layout is built <strong>programmatically via the DOM API</strong>
        (no <code>.lst</code> or <code>.json</code> design file needed).
        See <code>Services/ReportService.cs</code> for details.
    </li>
    <li>
        Customer data lives in an <strong>in-memory list</strong> provided by
        <code>Services/CustomerDataService.cs</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
        The generated PDF is returned as a byte array and
        <strong>downloaded directly from the browser</strong> using JS interop —
        no file system access is needed.
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>WASM Limitations</h2>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Single-threaded by default.</strong>
        Report generation runs on the main thread. A loading spinner is shown
        while the export is in progress. Very large reports may briefly freeze
        the UI; for production use, consider offloading to a Web Worker.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>No host file system access.</strong>
        All I/O uses <code>MemoryStream</code>; the PDF is streamed directly
        to a browser download.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Initial load time.</strong>
        The SkiaSharp WASM binary adds several MB to the download. Enable
        Brotli compression on your web server to reduce the payload size.
    </li>
</ul>

<p>
    Head to the <a href="report">Report</a> page to generate a sample PDF.
</p>
